## CLI surface, read read-only before any step

`tools/tb qmark tb277 lldp1159 u2 115200 ...` — `<prefix> ?` typed with **no CR**, then the
line cleared with Ctrl-U. Each run began with the tool's own self-test:
`self-test OK: 'show clock ?' then Ctrl-U then CR executed nothing`. Nothing was executed.

**Exec mode**
```
show lldp  ?      interface | local-info | neighbors | statistics | <cr>
show lldp statistics  ?        interface | <cr>
show lldp neighbors  ?         detail | interface | <cr>
show lldp local-info  ?        base | dot1 | dot3 | med | interface | <cr>
show lldp interface  ?         IFRANGE
```
🔴 Confirming the queue's triage note: **`show lldp neighbors brief` does not exist.** The
forms that exist are the five above.

**Global configuration mode**
```
lldp  ?
  faststart-count                 Set the fast start count for LLDP-MED
  holdtime-multiplier             Is multiplied by the Tx interval to give the TTL value
                                  advertised to neighbors
  non-strict-med-tlv-order-check  Enable non-strict LLDP-MED TLV order checking
  notification-interval           The minimum interval between LLDP notifications
  port-number-type                The type of port identifier used to enumerate LLDP MIB
                                  local port entries
  reinit                          The minimum time after disabling LLDP on a port, before
                                  reinitialization is commenced
  run                             Enable LLDP operation
  timer                           The time interval between regular transmissions of LLDP
                                  advertisements to neighbors
  tx-delay                        The minimum time between transmitting LLDP advertisements
                                  due to a change in LLDP MIB content
lldp timer  ?                  <5-32768>  The interval in seconds
lldp holdtime-multiplier  ?    <2-10>     The multiplier factor
lldp tlv-select  ?             % Unrecognized command
```
🔴 **`lldp tlv-select` is NOT a global command on this build** — it is per-interface only.
A test design that assumed the global form would have failed at its first configuration step.

**Interface mode (`interface port1.0.10`)**
```
lldp  ?
  management-address  Management address to advertise to neighbors
  med-notifications   Enable sending LLDP-MED notifications
  med-tlv-select      The LLDP-MED TLVs to be transmitted to neighbors
  notifications       Enable sending LLDP SNMP notifications relating to this port or ports
  receive             Enable reception of LLDP advertisements from neighbors
  tlv-select          The TLVs to be transmitted to neighbors
  transmit            Enable transmission of LLDP advertisements to neighbors
lldp tlv-select  ?
  all | link-aggregation | mac-phy-config | management-address | max-frame-size |
  port-and-protocol-vlans | port-description | port-vlan | power-management | protocol-ids |
  system-capabilities | system-description | system-name | vlan-names
lldp med-tlv-select  ?
  all | capabilities | inventory-management | location | network-policy | power-management-ext
lldp transmit  ?               receive | <cr>
lldp notification  ?           <cr>
switchport voice  ?            dscp | vlan
```
⚠ Note the spelling: the help text for the interface-mode SNMP option reads **`notifications`**
(plural) while `lldp notification ?` also parses and offers `<cr>` — AW+ accepts the unique
prefix. The form this case sends is recorded with each step.

