The tree is a line — **swi_d —(port1.0.2)— swi_b —(port1.0.1)— swi_a** — so of swi_d's four
inter-switch links only port1.0.2 carries data. port1.0.4 and port1.0.14 (to swi_a) and
port1.0.16 (to swi_b) are **Alternate/Discarding**. port1.0.20 has no link at all and is the
control port for STEP 9. This table is recorded so a later flap is visible.

