### ✅ Was `lldp run` probe residue? No — it is the device's SAVED baseline

The dispatch asked this to be settled rather than assumed. It is settled by reading
**startup-config**, which no probe writes:

```
awplus#show startup-config | include lldp      (read as part of the full show startup-config)
lldp run
```
`lldp run` is present in `flash:/default.cfg`, the DUT's boot config — so it survives a reload
and it predates every probe this campaign ran. **The 11:59 probe did not put it there.** The
pre-case state of the subject is "LLDP globally enabled, all parameters default", and that is
the baseline this case restores to.

For completeness, startup-config also holds group A's saved underlay (`vlan 10
ckUNDERLAY-eth3`, `vlan 48 ckUNDERLAY-eth4`) and **does not** hold `vlan 60` or
`interface vlan60` — confirming the campaign note that vlan 60 was still unsaved when this
case began.

