# STEP 12 — 🔴 REBOOT PERSISTENCE, measured on the wire for the first time in three campaigns

**Why this step, and why it could not be done before.** Reboot persistence has come back
**NOT MEASURED** from T33380, T33386 and T47192, because proving it needs a `write` and a
`write` would have saved the shared `vlan 60`. The Test Engineer removed that bind at 14:0x on
2026-10-21: testers may `write` freely from group C onward, and he removes vlan 60 himself at
campaign end. This is the first case able to run the limb.

**The configuration chosen to persist** is deliberately distinct from the default **and** from
every value used earlier in this case, so that "it survived" cannot be confused with "it
reverted to a default that happens to look the same":

```
awplus(config)#lldp timer 15                     (default 30; STEP 8 used 10)
awplus(config)#lldp holdtime-multiplier 3        (default 4;  STEP 8 used 2)
awplus(config)#lldp notification-interval 10     (default 5)
awplus(config)#interface port1.0.10
awplus(config-if)#lldp tlv-select system-name    (default: no optional TLVs at all)
```
```
  Notification Interval ..... 10 secs     [5]
  Tx Timer Interval ......... 15 secs     [30]
  Hold-time Multiplier ...... 3           [4]
  (Computed TTL value ....... 45 secs)
```
Expected on the wire after the reboot, if it persists: frames every **15 s**, TTL **45 s**,
and a **System Name** TLV — a combination this DUT has produced at no other point in the case.

### What the `write` added to startup-config — read, not assumed

`show startup-config` was captured before and after the `write` and diffed. The complete
difference:
```
 ! Startup-config saved on Tue Oct 20 23:45:48 2026 +0000   ->  Wed Oct 21 02:34:10 2026 +0000
+lldp holdtime-multiplier 3
+lldp notification-interval 10
+lldp timer 15
+ vlan 60 name ckMGMT-A
- vlan 10,48 state enable      ->  + vlan 10,48,60 state enable
+interface port1.0.2
+ switchport mode trunk
+ switchport trunk allowed vlan add 60
+ lldp tlv-select system-name            (under interface port1.0.10)
+interface vlan60
+  ip address 10.38.22.97/27
```
Four lines are this case's own; the rest is **vlan 60**, the campaign infrastructure, landing
in startup-config **exactly as the Test Engineer's decision anticipated and accepted**. It is
recorded here so the campaign-end removal is unambiguous:
🔴 **swi_d's startup-config now contains `vlan 60` (`ckMGMT-A`, `10.38.22.97/27`, tagged on
port1.0.2). Removing it needs `no interface vlan60` / `no vlan 60`, which the permission system
refuses for a tester, so it is the Test Engineer's own hands at campaign wrap.**

### The reload

```
awplus#reload
reboot question: 'reboot system? (y/n):' -> y        (tools/tb ckreload, which answers `y` to
                                                      the reboot question and `n` to any
                                                      save-config question)
15:34:55 NZDT  reload issued
15:35:58 NZDT  login banner seen after 60 s
```
The console transcript shows a genuine cold start — the kernel banner, the switch ports
cycling through disabled state, the daemon list (`authd, irdpd, lacpd, lldpd, loopprotd,
mstpd, nsm, rmond, sflowd, imi, imiproxyd`) and `Loading configuration file
flash:/default.cfg, please wait. ... done!`. **60 s from `reload` to the login prompt** on this
platform.

### After the reboot — configuration

```
awplus#show running-config | include lldp
lldp holdtime-multiplier 3
lldp notification-interval 10
lldp timer 15
lldp run
awplus#show running-config interface port1.0.10
 lldp tlv-select system-name
awplus#show lldp
  Notification Interval ..... 10 secs     [5]
  Tx Timer Interval ......... 15 secs     [30]
  Hold-time Multiplier ...... 3           [4]
  (Computed TTL value ....... 45 secs)
awplus#show lldp interface port1.0.10
 1.0.10   Rx Tx  -- --  10.38.22.34      --Sn------ -------- -------- McNpLoPe--
```
All five configured items survived, including the per-interface TLV selection (`Sn` in the
Base column).

### After the reboot — ON THE WIRE, which is the actual verdict

```
pcap      /tmp/lldp1159/s12_persist.pcap
packets   4 total, 4 LLDP

source e2:1a:ea:d4:70:43 -> 01:80:c2:00:00:0e
  frames 4 over 45.0 s
  inter-frame gap  min 15.01 s  mean 15.01 s  max 15.01 s
  --- frame at 1792550268.079, 5 TLVs ---
    Chassis ID                         MAC address: e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43
    Port ID                            Interface name: port1.0.10
    Time To Live                       45 s
    System Name                        awplus
    OUI e01aea subtype 2               0c26573a87c541829d436cb04a0e77c2
```
**Every one of the three independent signatures is present after a cold boot:**

| persisted setting | predicted on the wire | measured |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `lldp timer 15` | 15 s between frames | **15.01 s**, four frames, no spread |
| `lldp holdtime-multiplier 3` | TTL = 15 × 3 = 45 | **45 s** |
| `lldp tlv-select system-name` | a System Name TLV, 5 TLVs not 4 | **System Name `awplus`, 5 TLVs** |

This is not a `show` command agreeing with itself after a reboot. It is the device behaving
differently on the wire, in three measurable ways at once, because of configuration that
survived a power-off-equivalent restart.

### Other things the reboot confirmed, free

- **Boot pointers unchanged:** `Current boot image : flash:/x960-tb277.rel (file exists)`,
  `Current boot config: flash:/default.cfg (file exists)`, `Autoboot status : disabled` — the
  gate-7 baseline, returned to.
- **The inherited underlay and vlan 60 survived**, because they too are now saved:
  `vlan10 10.38.22.34/27`, `vlan48 10.38.22.66/27`, `vlan60 10.38.22.97/27`, all
  `admin up / running`.
- **The neighbour table rebuilt itself** to the same four switch neighbours, so the partners
  re-advertised to a freshly booted DUT without any help.
- **swi_a and swi_b were not rebooted.** Only swi_d reloaded. The session constraint on swi_a
  was never approached.

### Restoration, and what startup-config holds now

```
awplus(config)#no lldp timer
awplus(config)#no lldp holdtime-multiplier
awplus(config)#no lldp notification-interval
awplus(config-if)#no lldp tlv-select system-name       (interface port1.0.10)
awplus#write
Building configuration...
[OK]
```
`show startup-config` diffed against the one taken after the test `write` — the **only**
changes are the four test lines being removed:
```
 ! Startup-config saved on Wed Oct 21 02:34:10 2026 +0000  ->  02:38:03 2026 +0000
-lldp holdtime-multiplier 3
-lldp notification-interval 10
-lldp timer 15
- lldp tlv-select system-name
```
Startup-config now holds exactly: group A's underlay, `lldp run` (its own pre-campaign
baseline), and vlan 60 — the accepted end state.

**STEP 12 verdict: PASS. Reboot persistence is MEASURED, not NOT MEASURED.**

