6. **Host legs re-ARPed after the reboot.** The first closing probe raised
   `[portlink] tb-swi_d eth3/eth4 CHECK_CABLE — NIC has link but its MAC was not learned on
   any switch port`. That is a consequence of **my own reload** emptying swi_d's MAC table,
   not a cable fault: `tools/tb ping tb277 eth3 10.38.22.34 3` and
   `tools/tb ping tb277 eth4 10.38.22.66 3` both returned **3/3, 0% loss**, and the next probe
