   ```
     /dev/u2: ok baud=115200 banner=awplus hostname=awplus
   capturing 7 commands on 1 device(s) ...
   MATCH -- the bench equals the template.
   ```
   **Exit 0 MATCH.**

   The template for this check is a swi_d-only cut of the run `.setup`, written because
   **u3 and u5 could not be opened at hand-back** — both consoles are locked out, and the
   sentinel's standing instruction for this group is that nothing touches them, since every
   attempt re-arms the five-minute lock. A probe naming them can only report them missing.
   For completeness, the probe **was** first run against the full three-unit run `.setup` and
   returned 11 `MISSING_IN_LIVE` rows, every one of them for swi_a or swi_b and every one of
   them a consequence of not opening those consoles — **no row described swi_d or either host
   leg**. The repo's `bench-setup/tb277/bench-state.md` was **not** overwritten: both probes
   wrote to `/tmp`.
8. **Nothing left running on the box.** Every capture was a bounded `timeout <secs> tcpdump`
